        <li><span class="tag tag--early">EARLY</span> — the rails are live, the money is thin</li>
        <li><span class="tag tag--long-odds">LONG ODDS</span> — the winners are real, the median is roughly $0</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    {LANES.map((lane, i) => (
      <section class="lane" id={lane.key}>
        <header class="lane__head">
          <h2 class="lane__title"><span class="lane__num mono">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span> {lane.title}</h2>
          <p class="lane__count mono">{byLane[lane.key]?.length ?? 0} routes</p>
        </header>
        <p class="lane__intro">{lane.intro}</p>
        <div class="routes">
          {(byLane[lane.key] ?? []).map((e) => (
            <article class={`route route--${e.tier}`}>
              <header class="route__head">
                <span class={`tag tag--${e.tier}`}>{tierLabel(e.tier)}</span>
                {e.url ? (
                  <h3 class="route__name"><a href={e.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{e.name} ↗</a></h3>
                ) : (
                  <h3 class="route__name">{e.name}</h3>
                )}
                <span class="route__operator mono">{e.operator}</span>
              </header>
              <dl class="route__facts">
                <div>
                  <dt class="mono">THE WORK</dt>
                  <dd>{e.work}</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt class="mono">THE PAY</dt>
                  <dd>{e.pay}</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt class="mono">GETTING IN</dt>
                  <dd>{e.getIn}</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt class="mono">THE CATCH</dt>
                  <dd class="route__catch">{e.catchLine}</dd>
                </div>
              </dl>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    ))}

    <section class="graveyard">
      <p class="kicker">THE GRAVEYARD · LANES THAT MOSTLY NEVER PAID</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>The GPT Store.</strong> Revenue sharing was announced in
          January 2024 as a US-only pilot and never really shipped. Builders
          who did get paid report hundreds of dollars total. A marketplace
          announcement is not an income stream.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Selling prompts.</strong> PromptBase gives sellers 80%,
          and its top sellers land $200–400/month; of every 1,000 published
          prompts, about 20 ever make a sale. Etsy banned prompt bundles
          outright. Models also keep getting better at prompting themselves.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Generalist "AI tutor" jobs at the labs.</strong> xAI laid
          off ~500 generalist tutors in late 2025 and later paused tutor
          hiring entirely while surging specialists. The bottom of this
          market is being automated by the thing it trains.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="smells">
      <p class="kicker">SMELL TEST · WHEN TO WALK</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Anyone charging you to apply.</strong> The vetting is unpaid everywhere on this page — that's the honest version. Paying to be vetted is the tell.</li>
        <li><strong>Guaranteed income, dashboard screenshots, first-name case studies.</strong> The verifiable numbers in this guide came from platform filings and marketplace transaction data; screenshots are free to fabricate.</li>
        <li><strong>Courses about making money with AI.</strong> Usually the course <em>is</em> the business, and you are the revenue. Everything worth knowing about a platform is on the platform.</li>
        <li><strong>Anything that only works before everyone finds out.</strong> The build cost went to zero for everyone at once. Moats now are distribution, credentials, or taste — nothing a course can hand you.</li>
        <li><strong>Plans that assume smooth income.</strong> Every lane here is lumpy — empty queues, vanished projects, policy shifts. Plan for the gaps or the gaps plan for you.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <aside class="surfaces">
